# Ignore all files in tmp (plan artifacts, logs, and local scratch)
tmp/

# agentteams update/migration backups (local rollback artifacts)
.github/agents/.agentteams-backups/

# Python package build and virtual environment artifacts
.venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Archival update backups (any location) — never tracked (update-policy)
**/.agentteams-backups/

# agentteams local artifacts — do not commit
.agentteams-backups/
.agentteams-fleet/
bridge-*.report.md
**/bridge-*.report.md
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.prelabel.bak
.DS_Store

# researchteam layer-1 union temp descriptor (created+removed during agentteams merge)
.rt-descriptor-*.json

# Per-project literature library — optional out-of-band full-text corpus + bulky vector store are
# regenerable and never committed (the durable pins are literature.jsonl + *.provenance.json).
# The base index (literature.jsonl / term-vectors.jsonl / library-manifest.json) IS committed.
# See docs/literature-library-protocol.md.
**/references/library/corpus/*.txt
**/references/library/vectors/store/

# agentteams code & API index (F-CODEIDX) — a gitignored local cache (manifest.json + per-kind
# partitions) that embeds machine-specific resolved paths/versions; regenerable, NEVER committed and
# NEVER drift-tracked. Both patterns are load-bearing: the root-anchored one, and the `**/` one that
# matches the actual cache location `.github/agents/references/code-index/`. Query-time staleness keeps
# it fresh. See docs/retrieval-surfaces.md and docs/code-index-integration-plan.md.
references/code-index/
**/references/code-index/

# agentteams autosync gate — transient PR-body scratch (never committed)
.autosync-pr-body.md
**/.autosync-pr-body.md

# Full-text source corpus (retrieval surface #5) — the extracted text, per-chunk/per-page rows and
# the vector store are large, high-churn, machine-local and regenerable from sources/ +
# scripts/build_source_corpus.py. The COMMITTED durable layer is the compact manifests
# (sources-manifest.jsonl, corpus-extract-manifest.json, corpus-vector-manifest.json,
# quality-manifest.json) plus the dedup/triage report and the bibliography.
#
# These live UPSTREAM deliberately. .gitignore is a layer-2 MANAGED file: `researchteam update`
# overwrites it wholesale from upstream with no merge, so a pattern that exists only in a derived
# repo is silently deleted on the next sync. On 2026-08-07 that is exactly what happened in
# SocialScienceHumanities — the sync dropped these lines and exposed 1041 corpus files (198 MB)
# that had been correctly ignored moments before. A derived-only ignore pattern is not durable;
# it has to be here.
**/references/corpus/text/
**/references/corpus/vectors/
**/references/corpus/chunk-texts.jsonl
**/references/corpus/chunks.jsonl
**/references/corpus/quality.jsonl

# LaTeX build droppings under Projects/ — regenerable compiler output, never source of truth. The
# .tex source and the built .pdf/.html are the deliverables and stay tracked; these do not.
Projects/**/*.aux
Projects/**/*.log
Projects/**/*.toc
Projects/**/*.synctex.gz
